[O]No blade on the first kill: abandon the chain, do not wait for him again [QS610] [G27.4,69.4 Stranglethorn Vale]
[O]At [TAR2542 Catelyn the Blade], [QT610] (2,250 XP) [QA611 The Curse of the Tides] (3,150 XP: destroy the Altar of the Tides with her blade, kill Gazban and bring the Stone of the Tides back to the Baron - on the way to the dungeon) [G27.3,77.5 Stranglethorn Vale]

[OC]|cffffffffThe Drowned City|r  -  |cFFFF0000GROUP 3+|r, required. Forever caps the instance at 5: bring the tank friend and a healer. Food, water and repair in Booty Bay first. The quests are level 40; the layout, the bosses, the mob levels and where the tablets stand are not in any data file. About 9,400 plain quest XP rides on the run (with Dibbs' follow-up) and up to 13,300 more on the optional quests. Your quests, with the honest label:
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Take Two With Water (95787) - rubbings of the four Tablets of I'lalai - |cff66ff66normal|r: use the hide and charcoal on each tablet (the data names neither the hide and charcoal nor where the tablets stand)
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r The Saltseer Captain (95791) - 3 Saltseer Coroners and Captain Dreadrise - |cff66ff66normal|r
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Shady Saltseers (95789) - 10 Voodoo-Infused Artifacts - |cffffcc00grind|r: about 40% from each Saltseer pirate (Murderer, Cultist, Manhunter, Coroner), ~25 kills, and the run's own Saltseer kills count. One run: short at the exit = abandon
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Magics of the Drowned City (95788) - 5 I'lalai Fetishes - |cFFFF0000luck, do not farm it|r: 9-17% from Risen Sentries, Profane Necromancers and Undying Offerings (~30-55 kills for 5). One run: short at the exit = abandon
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Ancient Gurubashi Secrets (97130, only if you took it from Timear) - the Ancient Gurubashi Idol - |cffffcc00luck|r: the data does not say whether an object or a boss gives it. One run only
[O]On the way north, at the Altar of the Tides use Catelyn's Blade on it, then kill [TAR2624 Gazban] (level 40) for the Stone of the Tides [QC611] (the altar-then-Gazban order is Classic knowledge, unverified) [G25.0,23.6 Stranglethorn Vale]
|cFFFF0000GROUP 3+|r Swim north past the Vile Reef to the Sunken Hollow by the isle of water elementals and enter the underwater cave beside a large stone tablet (community guides; the entrance is not in the data and is unverified in game). Water Breathing helps [G21.4,27.9 Stranglethorn Vale]
Use the hide and charcoal on the four Tablets of I'lalai to make the rubbings (|cff66ff66normal|r) [QC95787] [G21.4,27.9 Stranglethorn Vale]
Kill 3 [TAR260353 Saltseer Coroner] and [TAR260042 Captain Dreadrise] (|cff66ff66normal|r; the data also lists a second Captain Dreadrise, 270884) [QC95791] [G21.4,27.9 Stranglethorn Vale]
[O]Kill [TAR270912 Saltseer Manhunter] and the other Saltseer pirates for 10 Voodoo-Infused Artifacts [QC95789] (~40% - budget ~25 kills) [G21.4,27.9 Stranglethorn Vale]
[O]Kill [TAR258792 Risen Sentry], Profane Necromancers and Undying Offerings for 5 I'lalai Fetishes [QC95788] (9-17% - luck: only the kills the run already makes) [G21.4,27.9 Stranglethorn Vale]
[O]Loot the Ancient Gurubashi Idol if the run gives it [QC97130] [G21.4,27.9 Stranglethorn Vale]
[O]At the exit with fewer than 10 artifacts: abandon Shady Saltseers, never a re-run [QS95789] [G21.4,27.9 Stranglethorn Vale]
[O]At the exit with fewer than 5 fetishes: abandon Magics of the Drowned City, never a re-run [QS95788] [G21.4,27.9 Stranglethorn Vale]
[O]If you hold The Web of Magic from chapter 27 and it still asks for a fetish you do not have: abandon it [QS95798] [G21.4,27.9 Stranglethorn Vale]
[O]No idol: abandon Ancient Gurubashi Secrets [QS97130] [G21.4,27.9 Stranglethorn Vale]

